rolls","description":"Wake Forest dominated SMU on the gridiron Saturday -- and added insult to injury after the game.","published":"2026-11-15T05:30:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481104/college-football-trolls-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the winningest college football coaches of all time?","description":"From Saban to Paterno, there are many legendary college football coaches. Who has the best career record? Check out who has the most wins now.","published":"2026-11-15T04:25:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/39283806/who-winningest-college-football-coaches-all","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Louisville holds off UNC in game that ends with brawl","description":"Louisville held off North Carolina 16-14 on Saturday night in a game that ended in a brawl and each of the teams having to be separated.","published":"2026-11-15T04:55:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50486992/louisville-holds-unc-game-ends-brawl","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kentucky's CFP hopes take hit in upset loss to Gators, Philo","description":"Florida quarterback Aaron Philo had 221 all-purpose yards and a touchdown to rally the Gators past No. 11 Kentucky 21-14 Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T04:13:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50486400/kentucky-cfp-hopes-take-hit-upset-loss-gators-philo","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 24 Boise State outlasts Oregon State, to host Pac-12 title game","description":"Rasean Jones caught 11 passes for 230 yards and 3 TDs to help No. 24 Boise State outlast Oregon State 46-41 and wrap up the host spot in the Pac-12 title game.","published":"2026-11-15T03:30:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50486399/boise-state-outlasts-oregon-state-host-pac-12-title-game","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 16 Oregon keeps CFP hopes alive with win over Michigan","description":"Dylan Raiola threw for 341 yards and four touchdowns, and No. 16 Oregon kept its slim chances for a spot in the College Football Playoff alive with a victory over struggling Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T03:15:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50485510/no16-oregon-keeps-cfp-hopes-alive-win-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Grant Wilson delivers as Indiana boosts CFP, Big Ten hopes with win vs. USC","description":"With Grant Wilson filling in at quarterback, No. 9 Indiana ramped up its offensive attack against USC and scored its best win of the season Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T03:22:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50485076/grant-wilson-indiana-boost-cfp-big-ten-hopes-win-vs-usc","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4921117/vicari-swain","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicari_Swain"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Vicari Swain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicari_Swain","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:07Z","intro":"Vicari S. Swain (born September 12, 2004) is an American college football cornerback and return specialist for the South Carolina Gamecocks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Swain grew up in Carrollton, Georgia, and started playing football at age six. He attended Central High School where he competed in football and baseball and was a top defensive back and wide receiver in the former. As a junior, he posted 55 receptions for 855 yards and eight touchdowns along with 28 tackles and six interceptions. Swain then recorded 44 receptions for 610 yards and seven touchdowns along with 35 tackles and six interceptions as a senior in 2022. A four-star recruit, he committed to play college football for the South Carolina Gamecocks."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Swain appeared in three games for the Gamecocks as a true freshman in 2023. He then made 13 appearances as a backup cornerback in 2024, recording 13 tackles and a sack. He became a top cornerback and return specialist for the Gamecocks in 2025. In the first two games, Swain had three punt return touchdowns, earning Southeastern Conference (SEC) Special Teams Player of the Week both times. He returned a total of 19 punts for 302 yards and three touchdowns during the season, tying Kaden Wetjen for most punt return touchdowns nationally. He also posted 28 tackles, five pass breakups and two interceptions on defense."}]}}